{"content":[{"c":["GOLIATH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Eleventh-century ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," Philistine warrior from Gath, who challenged Israel to battle (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.17.1-58","r":"1Sam.17.1-58","rawR":"1Sam.17.1-58","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.17.1-58","value":"1Sam.17.1-58"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 17"},"). He was subsequently felled and decapitated by the youthful David. Goliath was over nine feet (2.7 meters) tall, wore armor weighing about 125 pounds (56.8 kilograms), and carried a spear of 15 pounds (6.8 kilograms) weight. His sword, kept at Nob, was later given to David (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.21.9","r":"1Sam.21.9","rawR":"1Sam.21.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.21.9","value":"1Sam.21.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 21:9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.22.10","r":"1Sam.22.10","rawR":"1Sam.22.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.22.10","value":"1Sam.22.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:10"},"). He may have descended from the Anakim (see ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.11.22","r":"Josh.11.22","rawR":"Josh.11.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.11.22","value":"Josh.11.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 11:22"},"), but his height could have resulted from an anterior pituitary tumor. In ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.21.19","r":"2Sam.21.19","rawR":"2Sam.21.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.21.19","value":"2Sam.21.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Samuel 21:19"}," his death is attributed to Elhanan, who in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.20.5","r":"1Chr.20.5","rawR":"1Chr.20.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.20.5","value":"1Chr.20.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 20:5"}," is credited with killing Goliath’s brother."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Goliath","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Sm 17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.17.1-58","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.17.1-58","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.17.1-58"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 21:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.21.9","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.21.9","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.21.9"},{"anchorText":"22:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.22.10","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.22.10","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.22.10"},{"anchorText":"Jos 11:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.11.22","rawQueryValue":"Josh.11.22","sourceRefExact":"Josh.11.22"},{"anchorText":"2 Samuel 21:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.21.19","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.21.19","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.21.19"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 20:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.20.5","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.20.5","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.20.5"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"372b162f641d025478400bf0fc566e29ed21687c48ab54a8f7d85d94cbbf92f7","sourceItemName":"Goliath","sourceItemOrder":183,"sourceMember":"Articles/G.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Goliath","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Goliath","title":"Goliath","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}